\section{Credentials}{

With no key, calls are anonymous and use the Free tier, which is valid and
never an error by itself. The key is sent as the \code{X-API-Key} header, only to
the configured base URL (a redirect to another host drops it), and never
appears in printed output, logs or error messages.

The open routes (\code{\link[=ew_search]{ew_search()}}, \code{\link[=ew_catalog_location]{ew_catalog_location()}},
\code{\link[=ew_catalog_station]{ew_catalog_station()}} and \code{\link[=ew_attribution]{ew_attribution()}}) are sent \strong{without} the
key even when the client has one, so every caller shares one entry in the
API's edge cache. Set \code{send_key_on_open_routes = TRUE} to attribute every
request to your key instead.
}

\section{Cache}{

Responses are kept in an in-memory cache (256 entries, 32 MiB) keyed by the
full URL and a SHA-256 digest of the API key (never the key itself), and
revalidated with \code{If-None-Match} on every call: an unchanged forecast then
costs a \verb{304 Not Modified} and no download. Pass \code{cache = FALSE} to turn it
off, or a cache object to share one between clients or sessions: the
result of \code{\link[=ew_memory_cache]{ew_memory_cache()}}, or any object with \verb{$get(key)},
\verb{$set(key, value)} and \verb{$remove(key)} methods, such as a
\code{cachem::cache_disk()}.
}

\section{Retries}{

Connection errors (except TLS verification failures) and HTTP 429, 502,
503 and 504 are retried up to \code{max_retries} times. After a 429 or 503 with
\code{Retry-After}, the client waits exactly that long (up to 60 seconds; a
longer wait is returned as the error instead). Otherwise it waits a random
time between 0 and \code{min(8, 0.5 * 2^(n - 1))} seconds before retry \code{n}.
Nothing else is retried.
}

